      "writtenOn": "2020-05-03T04:08:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "At the point in this chain where I wrote code to index SVIDs (mode discovery), I actively avoided reading from this field, because it was unclear to me what exactly \"currently being operated on\" meant. Also, as you point out, it is unaware of SOP/SOP\u0027. I instead look up the next SVID to discover modes for when I need it. Hopefully, this will meet with your approval.\n\nI retained the writes to svid_idx that I encountered, because I didn\u0027t want to disturb its consumers. dfp_consume_modes increments it, and dfp_discover_modes reads it. Those are straightforward and could be changed to use the new interface, assuming it passes review. process_tbt_compat_discover_modes decrements it for reasons that are non-obvious to me.",
      "parentUuid": "1d82fdf0_ac15a5a2",
      "range": {
